From ba81404cf244dce043a3ef6fd2e4e15426303479 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Duron27 <duron27@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:30:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 63/63] A normal quit is told to the server: net.setFarewell, a
 bye message, no 90 s hold

- Net::Sockets::setFarewell / net.setFarewell(id, line): a line sent on the connection, best effort and without
  blocking, when the Sockets are destroyed (the game quits). Not sent for close(), closeAll() or an unloaded game
- netlib registers {"t":"bye"} on every connection; the relay marks the player as leaving and, when the socket closes,
  removes them at once (out of party, others told) instead of keeping their place for the grace period
- TODO.md: item done

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
